      "name": "on_attest_reply",
      "message": {
        "defined": "AttestReply"
      },
      "receiver": "vault PDA",
      "from": "attest program header PDA of the pinned instance",
      "doc": "Dispatched before ConsumerMsg when the sender is the attest program."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Hand-written for LEZ v0.4 actor-model programs (see docs/DECISIONS.md D-MOD-4). Types, variants, field order, error codes and seed tags are generated from the Rust source by idl/gen_idl.py; one wire message type per program, borsh-encoded, enum tag = variant_index (u8). Extra keys (variant_index, doc, internal, sender, events, callbacks, notes, seed transform) are outside SPEL's schema and ignored by its serde types. PDA derivation differs from SPEL's documented one: here seed = sha256(const tag bytes || each part's raw bytes) (u64 = 8 bytes LE, no zero-padding to 32), address = AccountId::for_public_pda(program, seed). 'transform: keccak256' = keccak256 of the argument. eth_receiver and erc20_receiver share this message enum; eth_receiver pins token = 0xff..fe (EIP-7708) at InitVault and refuses InitPrivateVault. PDAs are derived under the consumer program id."
}
